+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry is the validation boundary between model-produced tool calls and consumer-provided executors.
+
+## Execution contract
+
+- Input that fails the resolved tool definition's JSON Schema is returned as a `ToolResponse` before the executor runs; required properties, declared types, and enums are enforced, and the result identifies the failing property path and constraint without including property values. ([validated by: returns value-redacted schema errors without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14))
+
+- Schema-valid input, including unknown properties, reaches the executor unchanged exactly once, so validation does not coerce values or apply defaults. ([validated by: returns value-redacted schema errors without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14))
+
+## Definition lifecycle
+
+- A static definition's schema is compiled during `register`, so an invalid schema throws then and names its tool. ([validated by: rejects broken static schemas at registration and validates each dynamic definition as resolved](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46))
+- A function-valued definition is resolved and validated against the schema current for each execution, while schema compilation may be cached by resolved schema-object identity. ([validated by: rejects broken static schemas at registration and validates each dynamic definition as resolved](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46))
+- An unknown tool name remains an exception. ([validated by: rejects broken static schemas at registration and validates each dynamic definition as resolved](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46))
